<title>USA: U.S. FAA proposes to fine McDonnell Douglas.</title>
<headline>U.S. FAA proposes to fine McDonnell Douglas.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Aviation Administration on Friday proposed a $229,000 fine against McDonnell Douglas Corp for allegedly failing to ensure that a number of skilled workers were properly certified.</p>
<p>It said McDonnell Douglas failed to maintain its quality control system and follow approved procedures to make sure that such critical operations as soldering and sealing were done by trained and periodically certified workers.</p>
<p>The FAA said the allegations involved work done between 1992 and 1994 and was unaware of any safety problems attributed to the alleged violations.</p>
</text>
